      "side": 0,
      "message": "Oh, I see the issue is that SkJpegCodec implicitly declares an inline virtual destructor. (This requires any TU which includes it to generate a default implementation.) Instead, SkJpegCodec should declare its destructor (as override) and define it in SkJpegCodec.cpp.\n\nLocally, declaring `~SkJpegCodec() override;` below and then adding `SkJpegCodec::~SkJpegCodec() \u003d default;` (right after the constructor) to SkJpegCodec.cpp makes everything work out more nicely. The decoder target then correctly hides its implementation details, and iwyu correctly starts pointing out that JpegDecoderMgr needs only be forward declared. (And there\u0027s no need for any awkward build changes.)\n\nThere\u0027s no downside to doing any of this, since ~SkJpegCodec is already virtual. And there is the upside of the linker not needing to clean up the mess of all the generated destructors.",
      "parentUuid": "7082c1aa_42fa3c21",
